# nr-office-engine-inspect: the inspection actions of the office engine (modules mixdog-office::inspect and mixdog-office::inline_audit)

Written without cargo: nothing below has been compiled (rustfmt parsed every file). The modules are a library the Office tool's service
(a later task of the office track) calls; this task registers no protocol method and no service, so nothing is removed from
SERVICE_PENDING in compose_flip.rs.

## native/core/crates/mixdog-office/src/lib.rs
After `pub mod snapshot;` (added by the nr-office-engine-snapshot fragment; after `pub mod session;` if that one is not applied yet) add, and
extend the crate documentation by one line ("[`inspect`] answers `issues`, `validate`, `get` and `query`; [`inline_audit`] is the measured read
that rides on every mutating action."):

    pub mod inline_audit;
    pub mod inspect;

## native/core/crates/mixdog-office/Cargo.toml
Nothing new beyond the nr-office-engine-snapshot fragment: the modules use mixdog-fsio, mixdog-js, mixdog-office-base, mixdog-rt (already in the
manifest) and mixdog-office-com, mixdog-office-pdf, mixdog-office-quality, mixdog-ooxml (the snapshot fragment adds them; mixdog_ooxml::soffice and
mixdog_ooxml::ooxml_validator are modules of the last). The twin test uses, as dev-dependencies, mixdog-fonts and mixdog-pdf (the snapshot
fragment) and mixdog-rt with `test-support` (in the manifest). No external crate enters the lock; Cargo.lock and the workspace-hack are unchanged.

